e on the outside of the computer. Software ports are the numbered gateways in programs that software programs use to exchange information.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="93737">port</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="sq"><ntig><termGrp><term id="480556">portë</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ALB</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="38600_2244485_2254828"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The Design feature that allows users to save particular Designs, Styles, or Structures for easy use or access later.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2244485">Favorites</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="sq"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2254828">Të parapëlqyerit</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ALB</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="38601_2244486_2254994"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The navigation layout that presents content in a single column on the page and that allows user to navigate from top to bottom.​​</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2244486">Vertical</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="sq"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2254994">Vertikal</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ALB</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun<