 to access the apps installed on their phone or other mobile device.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2902294">Apps</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Plural</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="sq"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2902998">Aplikacionet</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ALB</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Plural</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="51615_2902485_2917968"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A color variation of Xbox Wireless Controllers; universally understood black color pigment, bold and reflecting little light.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2902485">Carbon Black</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="sq"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2917968">Carbon Black</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ALB</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="51616_2902486_2918250"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A color variation for Xbox Wireless Controllers; universally understood blue color pigment of a medium tone, and not as warm as cobalt blue.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2902486">Shock Blue</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="sq"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2918250">Shock Blue</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ALB</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</t