sages disguised as trustworthy communications from well-known businesses. The name is a combination of the words “SMS” and “phishing”.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="3057907">smishing</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="sq"><ntig><termGrp><term id="3058303">SMS mashtruese</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ALB</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="53714_3120734_3121461"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The program that enables ISVs to build across the Microsoft Cloud, publish, and grow in the commercial marketplace.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="3120734">ISV Success</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="sq"><ntig><termGrp><term id="3121461">ISV Success</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ALB</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="53715_3057909_3058306"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The Microsoft Philanthropies program that provides technology grants and discounts to nonprofit organizations all over the world.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="3057909">Tech for Social Impact</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="sq"><ntig><termGrp><term id="3058306">Teknologji për impakt shoqëror</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ALB</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="53716_3057910_3058309"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A series of games or contests in Microsoft Teams that make up a single unit of competition to promote new learnings and healthy usage of tools and scenarios across the organization.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="3057910">tournament</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="sq"><ntig><termGrp><term id="3058309">turne</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ALB</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="53717_3057911_3058294"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The Microsoft Teams feature that intelligently arranges meeting elements for optimal viewing by automatically adjusting the layout when people join, turn on the video, or present.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="3057911">Dynamic view</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="sq"><ntig><termGrp><term id="3058294">pamje dinamike</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ALB</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="53718_3057912_3058298"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">In Microsoft Teams, a one-touch experience for joining third-party online meetings.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="3057912">one-touch join</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="sq"><ntig><termGrp><term id="3058298">hyrje me një prekje</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ALB</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="53719_3057913_3058293"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A feature in the Microsoft Teams calls app that allows users to combine calls together.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="3057913">call merge</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="sq"><ntig><termGrp><term id="3058293">bashkim thirrjesh</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ALB</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="53720_3057914_3058295"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The Microsoft Teams feature that allows users to seamlessly move their calls between different devices, such as from the laptop to a mobile phone and vice-versa, without any interruption in call service or quality.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="3057914">endpoint transfer</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="sq"><ntig><termGrp><term id="3058295">transferim pike fundore</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ALB</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><term